1
00:00:12,540 --> 00:00:22,320
All right, welcome back to Data Structures Land. Today we continue and complete our segment on binary trees. So this is part two.
欢迎回到数据结构乐园。今天继续二叉树部分。这是第二部分。

2
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:40,700
If you missed part one, go back and watch part one. Last time we talked about binary trees in general. We had each node stored an item, and also a left pointer and a right pointer to other nodes, and a parent pointer to another node.
如果错过第一部分请回去看。上次讨论了一般二叉树。每个节点存储了一个元素、左右指针和父指针。

3
00:00:41,220 --> 00:00:57,600
This was an example of a tree. B and C are A's children. A is the parents of B and C, and also the root of the entire tree. We defined the height of a node. We didn't use this too much yet, but we're going to use it a lot today. So remember, the height is as drawn in red here.
这是一个树的例子。B和C是A的子节点。A是父节点和根节点。我们定义了节点的高度，今天会大量用到。

4
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:20,100
Height of the node is the length of the longest downward path counting edges. So B, for example, has a length two path, so we write a two here. You can also think of it as if you just live within the subtree rooted at B, B's subtree, then what is the maximum depth of those nodes? If you prefer to think about it that way, either way is fine.
高度是最长向下路径的边数。B的路径长度为2。也可理解为子树中节点的最大深度。

5
00:01:20,640 --> 00:01:32,140
And in particular, we distinguished H, the height of the root node, as the height of the entire tree. And what we achieved last time was basically all of our operations ran in order H time.
根节点的高度H就是整棵树的高度。上次所有操作都在O(H)时间内运行。

6
00:01:33,020 --> 00:01:46,320
So we had subtree insert, subtree delete, subtree first and last. We could compute the predecessor and successor of a node all in order H time. So as long as H was small, we were happy.
有子树插入、删除、首末节点。可在O(H)内计算前驱和后继。只要H小就满意。

7
00:01:47,980 --> 00:02:04,320
And remember, what does predecessor and successor mean? It's talking about an implicit order in the tree, which is what we call traversal order, which is defined recursively as recursively traverse the left subtree, then output the root, then recursively traverse the right subtree.
前驱和后继指树中的隐含顺序——遍历顺序。递归定义：先左子树、然后根节点、再右子树。

8
00:02:05,180 --> 00:02:18,360
So in this example, the traversal order is F is the, if you go all the way left, that was the first in the traversal order. Then we have some space here.
例子中遍历顺序从F开始。一直向左走，F是第一个。

9
00:02:19,580 --> 00:02:22,020
Then we have D. Then we have B.
然后D。然后B。

10
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:35,620
Then we do the right subtree of B, which is E. Then we have the root, because we finished the left subtree of the root. So that's A. And then we have C.
然后B的右子树E。然后根节点A。然后C。

11
00:02:37,140 --> 00:02:50,040
So there's an implicit linear order encoded by this tree. And the whole point of binary trees is that we can efficiently update the tree much faster than we could explicitly write down an order in an array or something like that.
隐式线性顺序由树编码。二叉树的核心是比数组更快地更新顺序。

12
00:02:51,040 --> 00:03:00,240
So binary trees let us quickly. Now, quickly is not so quick right now, because everything is order H. And in the worst case, H is linear, because we could have a tree like this.
二叉树让我们快速操作。但还不够快——全是O(H)，最坏情况H是线性的。

13
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:17,680
But today, we're going to guarantee that H is log n. And so the goal of today is to take all of these operations that run in order H time and get them to run in order log n time, just by modifying the data structure we've already seen. So we've done a lot of the hard work.
但今天保证H=log n。将所有O(H)操作变成O(log n)，只需修改已有数据结构。

14
00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:41,980
Just a little bit more work we need to do today in something called AVL trees, or height balance. OK. But before we get there, I want to talk a little bit more. At the very end of last lecture, we talked about once you have these subtree operations, so I can insert and delete in the subtree, how do I actually use that to solve the problems that we care about in this class, which are sequence data structure and set data structure?
今天用AVL树或高度平衡来做。在那之前谈谈序列和集合问题：如何用子树操作解决它们？

15
00:03:43,460 --> 00:03:53,360
So we talked mostly about the set data structure last time. So in general, we're going to define what traversal order we maintain by a binary tree.
上次主要讲了集合数据结构。将由二叉树维护遍历顺序。

16
00:03:53,940 --> 00:04:08,210
And so for a set, because for the set interface, we're interested in doing queries like find next and find previous, given a key. If it's not there, tell me the previous one or the next one. This is something we could do with binary search.
对于集合关心查找后继和前驱。给定键不在时告诉我前一个或后一个。

17
00:04:08,880 --> 00:04:22,019
And so the big cool thing that binary trees let us do, if we let the traversal order always be all of the items stored in increasing key order, then we are effectively maintaining the items in order.
如果遍历顺序始终是递增键的顺序，就能有效按键的顺序维护元素。

18
00:04:23,940 --> 00:04:42,920
In a traversal order sense, again, we're not explicitly maintaining them in order. But up here, we're maintaining a tree that represents items in key order. And so this lets us do a subtree find operation, which you could easily use to implement find and find previous and so on. As follows,
我们维护表示键顺序的树，而非显式顺序。能做子树查找操作来实现查找和查找前驱。

19
00:04:43,360 --> 00:05:00,920
we start at the root of the tree. So we can say node equals root initially. And then we can recursively search for a key k as follows. We check, well, if the item at the root has a key that's bigger than k, let me draw a little picture.
从根节点开始，node=root。递归搜索键k。如果根节点键大于k。

20
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:16,440
So we're at some node here. This is a node. And it has a left subtree and a right subtree. And there's some item with some key.
我们在某个节点。有左子树和右子树，里面有带键的元素。

21
00:05:16,940 --> 00:05:32,090
So if the key we're looking for is less than the node's item, that means it's down here in the left subtree. And then we can recurse on node.left. If they're equal, that means that this item is the item we're looking for. So we can just return it or the node, depending on what you're looking for.
如果找的键小于节点键，在左子树中。递归到node.left。如果相等就返回该节点。

22
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:45,600
And if the key in here is greater than the key we're looking for, then we'll recurse to the right. If you think about it a little bit, this is exactly binary search on an array. It just happens to be on a tree instead.
如果键更大就递归到右边。这是数组上的二分查找，只是在树上。

23
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:47,480
If you think of an array,
想象一个数组。

24
00:05:54,300 --> 00:06:06,960
like this, where does binary search do? It first looks at the key in the middle. I'm going to draw that as the root. And then it recurses either on the left chunk, which I will draw recursively, or on the right chunk.
二分查找先看中间键，画成根节点。递归到左边或右边。

25
00:06:08,240 --> 00:06:18,980
And so if you happen to have a perfect binary tree like this one, it is simulating exactly binary search in this array. But this we're going to be able to maintain dynamically. Not perfect anymore, but close.
如果有完美二叉树，就在模拟二分查找。能动态维护——不再完美但很接近。

26
00:06:19,540 --> 00:06:22,000
Whereas this we could not maintain in sorted order.
而数组无法在有序下维护。

27
00:06:24,140 --> 00:06:38,080
This is like a generalization of binary search to work on trees instead of on arrays. And for this reason, set binary trees are called binary search trees, because they are the tree version of binary search. So there's many equivalent names.
这是二分查找从数组到树的推广。所以集合二叉树称为二叉搜索树。

28
00:06:38,760 --> 00:06:53,760
So binary search tree is another name for set binary tree. And the key thing that makes this algorithm work is so -called binary search tree property, which is all the keys in the left subtree of a node are less than the root of that node.
二叉搜索树的关键是BST性质：节点左子树的所有键都小于该节点。

29
00:06:54,220 --> 00:07:05,700
And that key is less than all the keys in the right subtree. And this is true recursively all the way down. And so that's how you prove that this algorithm is correct by this property. Why is this true?
该节点键小于右子树所有键，递归成立。这就是算法正确性的证明。

30
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:18,580
Because if we can maintain traversal order to be increasing key, then that's exactly what traversal order means. It tells you all the things in the left subtree come before the root, which come before all the things in the right subtree.
因为遍历顺序为递增键顺序，这正是遍历顺序的定义。

31
00:07:18,960 --> 00:07:21,740
So this property implies this one.
所以此性质蕴含彼性质。

32
00:07:23,940 --> 00:07:34,980
And how do you maintain things in increasing key order? It's pretty easy. If you want to insert an item, where does it belong? Well, you do this search to find where it would belong if it was there.
如何维护递增键顺序？插入元素时搜索它应在的位置。

33
00:07:35,540 --> 00:07:48,060
If it's there, you can overwrite the value stored with that key. If it's not, this search will fall off the tree at some point. And that's where you insert a new node in your tree.
如果在就覆盖。如果不在，搜索掉出树外的地方就是插入点。

34
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:58,140
That was covered in recitation, so I don't want to dwell on it. What I want to focus on today is the other application. This is for representing a set, which is relatively easy.
习题课已讲过。今天关注另一种应用——表示集合。

35
00:07:59,220 --> 00:08:09,120
A challenge, which we sort of set ourselves up for, but we need a little more work, is to make sequence binary trees. So suppose I have a binary tree.
挑战是序列二叉树。假设有二叉树。

36
00:08:09,540 --> 00:08:17,800
And what I would like, I mentioned at the end of last time, is that I want the traversal order of my tree to be the sequence order.
希望遍历顺序=序列顺序。

37
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:23,740
The order that I'm trying to represent is the one that's changed by operations like insert at.
顺序由插入等操作修改。

38
00:08:26,100 --> 00:08:39,039
So I'd just like to do the same thing. But now I have to think about how do I do a search, how do I do insert at, that sort of thing. And here is an algorithm for what I would like to work, but it's not going to quite work yet.
同样的事，但需要做搜索和插入——有一个算法还不能完全工作。

39
00:08:40,240 --> 00:08:48,360
So suppose I give you a subtree specified by a node. So there's all the descendants of that node.
假设给定一个由节点指定的子树及其所有后代。

40
00:08:51,320 --> 00:09:04,810
In the traversal order of that subtree, which starts here and ends here, and the root will be somewhere in the middle, give me the ith node. So if I ask i equals 0, I want to get this leftmost descendant.
在遍历顺序中找到第i个节点。i=0时最左边的后代。

41
00:09:05,340 --> 00:09:20,700
If I ask for i equals the size of the tree minus 1, I want to get the rightmost descendant. That was the first and last in the subtree that we talked about. But we know how to find the first and last. Just walk left or walk right. But we don't know how to find the ith node.
i=size-1时最右边的后代。知道如何找首末节点——向左或向右走到底。但不知道如何找第i个。

42
00:09:22,380 --> 00:09:32,370
And so I'm going to say, in order h times the goal right now, not log n. And the idea is, well, it seems like size matters. Sorry if you heard otherwise.
目前目标是O(h)。关键是大小很重要。

43
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:44,380
So in particular, I mentioned size when I was talking about the last node in the sequence. The index of that node is size of this subtree minus 1.
之前提到序列最后一个节点的索引是size-1。

44
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:48,020
So let's define the size of a node.
定义节点的大小。

45
00:09:51,400 --> 00:10:00,380
To be the number of nodes in its subtree. We're calling that subtree paren node.
子树中的节点数。称为子树父节点。

46
00:10:05,820 --> 00:10:17,470
OK. Including the node itself. So if I somehow knew the size, this seems important for understanding indexes. Let's just assume that I knew that magically in constant time.
包括节点本身。

47
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:25,300
Let's assume that the size of the left subtree. So why don't I expand this diagram a little bit.
假设知道左子树的大小。扩展一下图示。

48
00:10:28,960 --> 00:10:40,000
So we have node as before. But we have a left subtree and a right subtree. So this node here is node.left. This node here is node.right. They might not exist.
和之前一样有左右子树。node.left和node.right可能不存在。

49
00:10:40,880 --> 00:10:51,300
But let's ignore those exceptional cases for now. Let's suppose we knew not only the size of node, but we knew the size of node.left. So that is the size of this tree.
先忽略异常。假设知道node.size和node.left.size。

50
00:10:52,070 --> 00:11:02,560
So we have node.left. And we're going to call that, nl. So let's suppose that there are nl nodes down here. Well, I claim that lets me do the equivalent of a binary search.
node.left的size=nL。下面有nL个节点。这能做二分查找。

51
00:11:03,900 --> 00:11:15,580
Because I'm looking for some index i. And if i is less than nl, then I know that it must be down here. For example, if i equals 0, it's going to be in the left subtree as long as nl is greater than 0.
寻找索引i。如果i<nL就在左子树。i=0时在左子树。

52
00:11:16,760 --> 00:11:27,280
Right. So that's exactly this check. If i is less than nl, I'm going to recurse to the left subtree. To the left. Call subtree at of node.left, comma, i. So it's written here.
对。如果i<nL递归到左子树，调用subtree_at(node.left,i)。

53
00:11:27,920 --> 00:11:38,920
If i equals nl, if you think about it for a second. So nl is the number of nodes here. And so that means this node has index nl. The index of this node is nl.
如果i=nL，这个节点的索引就是nL。

54
00:11:39,680 --> 00:11:54,160
And so if the one index we're looking for is that one, then we just return this node. We're done. And otherwise, i is greater than nl. And that means that the node we're looking for is in the right subtree. Because it comes after the root.
如果要找的就是那个，直接返回。否则i>nL，节点在右子树中。

55
00:11:55,040 --> 00:12:12,020
Again, that's what traversal order means. So if we define it to be sequence order, then we know all the things that come after this node, which is index nl, must be over here. Now, when we recurse down here, our numbering system changes. Because for node, 0 is here.
这就是遍历顺序的意义。所有在索引nL之后的元素都在右边。递归到右边时编号变了。

56
00:12:12,460 --> 00:12:24,580
And then for node.right, 0 is here. So we need to do a little bit of subtraction here, which is when we recurse to the right, we take i minus nl minus 1. Minus nl for these guys, minus 1 for the root node.
对node.right，0在那。所以需要做减法：i - nL - 1。

57
00:12:26,140 --> 00:12:37,120
And that will give us the index we're looking for within this subtree. So my point is, this algorithm is basically the same as this algorithm. But this one uses keys.
得到要找的索引。这个算法和之前相同，只是用keys。

58
00:12:38,040 --> 00:12:49,580
Because we're dealing with a set. And in sets, we assume items have keys. Over here, items don't have to have keys. In fact, we're not touching the items at all. We're just asking, what is the ith item in my sequence?
是集合所以元素有键。对于序列不需有键，只需问第i个元素是什么。

59
00:12:51,320 --> 00:13:01,100
What is the ith item in my traversal order? Which is the same thing as asking, what is the ith node in the traversal order? And this algorithm gives it to you exactly the same way in order h time.
遍历顺序中第i个元素？算法在O(h)时间给出答案。

60
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:16,100
Now, I'm not going to show you all the operations. But you can use subtree at to implement get at and set at. You just find the appropriate node and return the item or modify the item.
可用subtree_at实现get_at和set_at。找到节点返回或修改元素。

61
00:13:17,340 --> 00:13:32,700
Or you can use it to, most crucially, you can use it to do insert at and delete at. This is a new thing we've never been able to do before. What do you do? Just like over here, if I'm trying to insert an item, I search for that item over here.
最关键：做insert at和delete at——以前从未能做到。

62
00:13:33,120 --> 00:13:37,660
So if I'm trying to insert at i, for example, I look for i. And then
在i处插入就找i。

63
00:13:40,620 --> 00:13:49,920
for insert at i, I want to add a new item just before that one. And conveniently, we already have, I didn't mention, but we have a subtree insert.
在位置i前添加新元素。已有子树插入操作。

64
00:13:51,320 --> 00:14:06,280
And we can add two versions, before and after. I think we covered after, which is successor, before we used predecessor. But we can just call subtree insert before at that node.
添加before和after两个版本。调用subtree insert before即可。

65
00:14:06,680 --> 00:14:17,400
And boom, we will have added a new item just before it. And great. So magically, somehow, we have inserted in the middle of the sequence.
在中间插入了新元素。

66
00:14:18,220 --> 00:14:26,880
And all of the indices update because I'm not storing indices. Instead, to search for an item at index i, I'm using the search algorithm.
所有索引更新因为没存索引——用搜索算法来找。

67
00:14:28,940 --> 00:14:32,340
But there's a problem. What's the problem?
但有个问题。

68
00:14:36,310 --> 00:14:48,760
This seems a little too good to be true. I insert in the middle of this tree. And then somehow, I can magically search and still find the ith item, even though all the indices to the right of that item incremented by 1.
好得不像是真的——插入后还能找到第i个？右边的索引都增加了1。

69
00:14:52,900 --> 00:14:54,640
It's almost true. Answer?
几乎是真的。回答？

70
00:14:58,160 --> 00:15:07,440
Yeah? Because we have to update the sizes. Right. I didn't say, how do I compute the size of the left subtree? So that is the next topic.
因为必须更新大小。如何计算左子树的大小？这是下个话题。

71
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:20,200
We're almost done. This will actually work. It's really quite awesome. But for it to work, we need something called subtree augmentation.
快完成了。这确实可行。但需要子树增广。

72
00:15:22,760 --> 00:15:25,580
Which I'll talk about generally. And then we'll apply it to size.
一般性地讲增广，然后应用到size上。

73
00:15:30,540 --> 00:15:43,260
So the idea with subtree augmentation is that each node in our binary tree can store a constant number of extra fields.
每个节点可存常数额外字段。

74
00:15:44,560 --> 00:16:11,980
Why not? And in particular, if these fields are of a particular type, or maybe I'll call them properties, I'm going to define a subtree property to be something that can be computed
称为属性。子树属性可从子节点属性计算。

75
00:16:21,580 --> 00:16:25,500
from the properties of the node's children.
从子节点属性计算。

76
00:16:28,640 --> 00:16:30,700
So I should say this is of a node.
这是指节点的。

77
00:16:36,690 --> 00:16:39,840
So children are node.left and node.right.
子节点是node.left和node.right。

78
00:16:41,880 --> 00:16:53,520
You can also access a constant amount of other stuff. For example, the node itself. But the point of a subtree property is it's downward looking. So I'm going to call it node.right.
子树属性是向下看的。

79
00:16:53,960 --> 00:16:53,960
And

80
00:16:56,260 --> 00:17:15,579
I want to compute some property about it. We want to store p of the node. And suppose we already know p over here, the property computed for the left subtree, or for the left node. And we already know the property for the right node.
要存储p(node)。假设已知左右节点的p。

81
00:17:15,940 --> 00:17:20,319
Then what I'd like is for this to be computable in constant time.
p(node)应在常数时间内可计算。

82
00:17:26,300 --> 00:17:36,580
So I can compute p of this node given p of the left node and p of the right node. That's a subtree property. Now in particular, size is a subtree property.
可由左右p计算出。这就是子树属性。size是其中之一。

83
00:17:37,980 --> 00:17:47,840
Why? Because I can write this kind of recurrence. Node.size equals node.left.size.
因为node.size = node.left.size + node.right.size + 1。

84
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:59,820
This is very tedious to write. So node.right.size plus 1.
写起来繁琐。node.right.size + 1。

85
00:18:04,220 --> 00:18:15,860
Thank you. Size of the entire subtree here, called node, is the size of the left subtree plus the size of the right subtree plus 1 for that node itself.
整棵子树的大小 = left + right + 1。

86
00:18:17,220 --> 00:18:24,940
So this is an update rule. Takes constant time to evaluate. It's two additions. Sorry, my t's look kind of like plus signs.
常数时间计算——两个加法。

87
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:29,420
The plus is a little bigger.
加号稍大。

88
00:18:35,680 --> 00:18:50,040
OK, so we're summing those three things. Boom, we can get node.size. So I claim that as long as my property has this feature, I can maintain it dynamically as I'm changing the tree.
三项加起来得到node.size。只要属性有这个特征就能动态维护。

89
00:18:50,600 --> 00:19:04,760
OK, now this is a little bit of a forward reference because we haven't said exactly how we're going to change the tree yet. But question? If node.size is recursive, how is it happening in constant time? Wouldn't it happen in? OK,
这是前向引用——还没说树怎么修改。如果node.size递归怎么常数时间？

90
