00:27:34,730 --> 00:27:54,020
OK. What does it mean for a property to be local to a subtree versus global? The best answer is this definition, but that's maybe not the most intuitive definition. This is what I mean. Something that can be computed just knowing information about your left and right children, that is the meaning of subtree property. And those are the only things you're allowed to maintain.
局部vs全局属性？可从左右子节点信息计算的即子树属性。

132
00:27:54,620 --> 00:28:12,620
Those are the only things that are easy to update by walking up this path. And the contrast is that a global property like index, it's global in particular, because I can do one change, add one node, and all of the node's properties change.
只有这些能通过向上走更新。全局属性如索引一次修改全变。

133
00:28:13,060 --> 00:28:22,500
So that's an extreme example of global. We want this very particular notion of local, because that's what we can actually afford to recompute.
全局的极端例子。我们要特定的局部概念。

134
00:28:23,680 --> 00:28:25,420
Hopefully that clarifies. Yeah?
希望说清楚了。

