00:34:43,889 --> 00:34:58,160
node dot left. Actually, I'd prefer to node dot right minus height of node dot left.

166
00:35:02,380 --> 00:35:08,720
So this thing is called skew of the node.
称为偏斜。

167
00:35:11,840 --> 00:35:14,840
And it's going to always be minus 1, 0, or plus 1.
始终在-1,0,+1之间。

168
00:35:17,840 --> 00:35:30,020
So this is saying that if I have any node, and I look at its left subtree and its right subtree, I measure their heights. Remember, that's downward distance, maximum distance to a leaf.
左右子树高度应相近。

169
00:35:30,820 --> 00:35:41,210
I measure the height of this tree, maximum height. I measure the maximum height of this subtree. I want these to be within one of each other. Ideally, they're equal. That would be the perfect case.
理想情况相等。

170
00:35:41,840 --> 00:35:53,340
But let's let them differ by 1. So maybe this is k, and this is k plus 1. Or maybe this is k, and this is k minus 1. In this picture, what is the height of this node?
允许相差1。这个节点的高度？

