00:41:00,400 --> 00:41:11,540
That this tree on height, if I take this tree versus this tree, this one has more nodes than this one. If I have larger height, this construction is going to build a bigger tree.
高度越大节点越多。

198
00:41:12,280 --> 00:41:23,680
At least as big. It doesn't even need to be strictly bigger. So certainly, n sub h minus 1 is greater than or equal to n sub h minus 2. Now this is 2 times n sub h minus 2.
N_{h-1} >= N_{h-2}。所以是2倍。

199
00:41:24,400 --> 00:41:36,900
And this is an easy recurrence. This is just powers of 2. I keep multiplying by 2 and subtracting 2 from h. So this solves to 2 to the h over 2, maybe with a floor or something.
简单递推——2的幂。解为2^{h/2}。

200
00:41:38,000 --> 00:41:48,690
But it is, I'm using a base case here, which is n sub 0 equals 1. Maybe it's a ceiling then. But the point is, this is exponential.
这是指数级。

201
00:41:49,480 --> 00:42:07,320
So this implies that the height is always at most 2 times log n. This 2 corresponds to this 2. If you just invert this formula, this was number of nodes is going to be at least 2 to the h over 2. And so h is at most 2 log n.
所以h <= 2 log n。

202
00:42:07,860 --> 00:42:18,800
So it's not log n. That would be perfect. But it's within a factor of 2 of log n. So AVL trees are always quite balanced. Number of levels is at most double what you need to store n nodes.
不正好log n但在2倍以内——足够平衡。

203
00:42:19,940 --> 00:42:20,180
Great.
好。

204
00:42:24,120 --> 00:42:33,860
We're left with the main magic. Not domain magic. That's different. And let's see. We're going to use subtree augmentation.
主要魔法是子树增广。

205
00:42:37,860 --> 00:42:37,960
That.

206
00:42:45,620 --> 00:42:55,440
Big remaining challenge is, how do we maintain this height balance property using rotations? We have all the ingredients lined up for us. We have subtree augmentation.
剩余挑战：如何用旋转维护高度平衡。

207
00:42:56,820 --> 00:42:57,860
What does that let me do?
能做什么？

208
00:43:00,940 --> 00:43:04,900
It's relevant to AVL trees. Well, it lets me store height.
存储高度。

209
00:43:07,860 --> 00:43:19,180
So to compute the height of a node, that in general, it takes linear time because I have to look at all the downward paths, all the leaves within that subtree. But height is a subtree property.
计算高度一般需线性时间——但高度是子树属性。

210
00:43:21,080 --> 00:43:25,120
So yes, height.
高度是。

211
00:43:27,660 --> 00:43:34,640
Why? Because let me just write it here. Node.height.
因为node.height = 1 + max(node.left.height, node.right.height)。

212
00:43:38,450 --> 00:43:44,420
Equals 1 plus max of node.left.height
1 + max(左高, 右高)。

213
00:43:49,300 --> 00:43:51,100
and node.right.height.
和右高。

214
00:43:56,060 --> 00:44:06,260
End of max. Let me put this in a box. This equation, or I guess it's an assignment operation. This is a 1.
这个公式——常数时间更新规则。

215
00:44:08,660 --> 00:44:18,440
It's the thing we've been doing over and over. When I said, what is the height of this node? You just figured that out. You took the height of the left subtree, maxed with the height of the right subtree, and added 1 to count for these edges.
一直都在做——左高和右高取最大加1。

216
00:44:19,180 --> 00:44:40,130
So this is a general update rule. It matches this subtree property pattern. If I have the property of left and right, I can compute it for node. And this takes constant time to do. And so it's a subtree property. And so I can maintain, through all the things I'm doing, the height of every node. Oh, by the way, whenever I do a rotation, I'm also going to have to update my subtree properties.
通用更新规则——常数时间。所以能维护每个节点的高度。

217
00:44:41,300 --> 00:44:51,560
When I rotate this edge, a does not change. b does not change. c does not change. So that's good. But x's subtree changes. It now has y it didn't before.
旋转后x的子树变了。

218
00:44:52,400 --> 00:45:01,670
So we're going to have to also update the augmentation here in y. And we're going to have to update the augmentation in x.
要更新y和x的增广。

219
00:45:02,760 --> 00:45:16,600
And we're going to have to update the augmentation of all of the ancestors of x. Eventually. So rotation is locally just changing a constant number of pointers. So I usually think of rotations as taking constant time.
最终更新x的所有祖先——旋转本身是常数时间。

220
00:45:18,180 --> 00:45:22,420
But eventually, we will have to do, this is constant time locally.
局部常数时间。

221
00:45:24,630 --> 00:45:27,790
But we will need to update
需要更新。

222
00:45:32,020 --> 00:45:40,340
h ancestors in order to store all of our augmentation operations up to date. We'll worry about that later.
更新h个祖先以保持增广最新。

223
00:45:43,620 --> 00:45:57,840
All right. So great. Now we have the height of all the nodes. We can compute the skew of all the nodes. Cool. We have this rotation operation. And we want to maintain this height balance property.
有高度就能计算偏斜。现在用旋转维护高度平衡。

224
00:45:58,560 --> 00:46:03,400
Height of left node, left and right of every node is plus or minus 1 or 0.
左右高度差在±1或0。

225
00:46:06,240 --> 00:46:06,620
Cool.
好。

226
00:46:09,260 --> 00:46:21,580
So I said over here somewhere, whenever we, so the only things that change the tree are when we insert or delete a new node. And the way that we implemented those so far is to add or remove a leaf.
唯一改变树的是插入或删除叶节点。

227
00:46:22,120 --> 00:46:34,860
So we should still be thinking about adding or removing a leaf. The problem is when I add a new leaf, now maybe this tree is higher than it used to be. So some node here may no longer be height balanced.
加叶节点后树可能变高，某些节点不再平衡。

228
00:46:35,420 --> 00:46:45,760
But because height is a subtree property, the only new nodes we need to check are the ones up this ancestor path. And there's only log n of them. Because now height is log n. That's what we just proved.
只需检查祖先路径——只有log n个。

229
00:46:46,540 --> 00:46:57,040
As long as we have this property. Now we right now don't have it for maybe these few nodes. But it will be, it was log n before. It's at most log n, 2 log n plus 1 right now. Because we just added a node.
现在是log n或2 log n+1。

230
00:46:58,220 --> 00:47:07,840
So what I want to do is check all of these ancestor nodes in sequence from bottom up. And find one that's out of balance. So let's take the,
从下到上检查所有祖先直到找到不平衡的。

231
00:47:11,730 --> 00:47:15,700
lowest out of balance node.
最低的不平衡节点。

232
00:47:21,600 --> 00:47:36,240
And I'm going to call that x. Now because we just insert or deleted a single leaf, it's only out of balance by 1. Because we only changed height, one height went up by 1 or one height went down by 1.
因为只增删一个叶节点，偏斜只差1。

233
00:47:36,800 --> 00:47:47,120
And before, all of our skews were plus or minus 1 or 0. So now, the bad case is when it's plus or minus 2. If it happens to still be in this range for all the nodes, we're happy.
坏情况是偏斜变成±2。

234
00:47:47,640 --> 00:47:57,380
But if it's outside this range, it's only going to be out by 1. So this means the skew is in plus 2 or minus 2.
偏斜为+2或-2。

235
00:47:58,680 --> 00:48:11,880
And let's say that it's 2 by symmetry. So my picture is, I'm going to draw. I'm going to draw a double right arrow to say that
设为+2。画双右箭头。

236
00:48:14,620 --> 00:48:24,720
this subtree is 2 higher than this subtree. So that's bad. And we want to fix it. The obvious thing to do is to rotate this edge.
这个子树高2——旋转修复。

237
00:48:25,520 --> 00:48:36,380
Because that'll make this, this is 2 high and this is 2 low. So if we rotate, this should go down by 1 and this should go up by 1. And that works most of the time.
旋转后高降低低升高。大多数情况有效。

238
00:48:38,260 --> 00:48:49,740
So case 1 is that skew of y. What is y? I want y to be the right child of x.
情况1：y是x的右子节点。

239
00:48:50,320 --> 00:49:04,020
Because we have positive skew, we know there is a right child. Now, because this was the lowest bad node, we know that y is actually good. It's either right heavy or even. The two subtrees have the same height or left heavy.
偏斜为正必有右子节点。y本身是好的。

240
00:49:04,840 --> 00:49:07,680
The easy case is, are
简单情况。

241
00:49:12,360 --> 00:49:17,180
when skew of y is either 1 or 0,
y的偏斜为1或0时。

242
00:49:21,780 --> 00:49:22,920
which I will draw.
画出来。

243
00:49:30,240 --> 00:49:34,620
So double right arrow. Let's say single right arrow.
双右箭头——单右箭头。

244
00:49:40,500 --> 00:49:45,640
So this, I'm just going to add some labels here to make this picture consistent.
加些标记使图一致。

245
00:49:48,980 --> 00:50:04,980
k plus 1, k plus 2. I'm writing the heights. So this is an example where c is taller than b. a and b are the same height. And then if you compute the heights up here, indeed, this one is right leaning. This one is doubly right leaning.
写高度——右倾和双右倾。

246
00:50:05,340 --> 00:50:14,220
Because this one has height k plus 1. This one has height k minus 1. That's bad. But if we do this right rotation on x, we get exactly what we want.
右旋x后得到所需结果。

247
00:50:18,040 --> 00:50:28,460
So I'm just going to copy the labels on a, b, c. We have k minus 1, k minus 1, and k. And then recompute. That means this guy has height k. This one has height k plus 1.
复制标记重算。

248
00:50:29,200 --> 00:50:40,960
And now, all the nodes in this picture that I've highlighted, a, b, and c haven't changed. They were height balanced before. They still are. But now, x and y. x wasn't height balanced before. y was. Now both x and y are height balanced.
a,b,c没变。x之前不平衡现在平衡了。

249
00:50:42,100 --> 00:50:51,700
That's case 1. In case 2, the skew of y is flat, which means that this is a k.
情况1。情况2：y偏斜为0。

250
00:50:52,300 --> 00:51:02,460
And this is a k. And this is a k plus 1. And this is a k plus 2. But still, all the nodes are balanced. Height balanced. They're still plus or minus 1.
所有节点仍平衡。

251
00:51:03,260 --> 00:51:11,320
So those are the easy cases. Unfortunately, there is a hard case. Case 3. But there's only one. And it's not that much harder.
简单情况。有且仅有一个难的情况3。

252
00:51:16,580 --> 00:51:19,460
So it's when skew of y is minus 1.
y偏斜为-1时。

253
00:51:21,920 --> 00:51:24,820
In this case, we need to look at the left child of y.
查看y的左子节点。

254
00:51:27,140 --> 00:51:31,800
And to be alphabetical, I'm going to rename this to z.
重命名为z。

255
00:51:33,990 --> 00:51:47,740
So this one, again, is double right arrow. This one is now left arrow. And this is letter y. And so we have a, b, c, and d.
双右箭头加左箭头。有a,b,c,d。

256
00:51:48,420 --> 00:52:01,800
Potential subtrees hanging off of them. And I'm going to label the heights of these things. These are each k minus 1 or k minus 2. This one's k minus 1. And now compute the insides.
标记高度。

257
00:52:02,420 --> 00:52:15,980
So this is going to be height k for this to be left leaning. So this is k plus 1. And this is k plus 2. But the problem is this is too higher than this. The height of z is too higher than the height of a.
z的高度比a高太多。

258
00:52:17,280 --> 00:52:28,420
In this case, if I do this rotation, things get worse, actually. I'll just tell you the right thing to do is this is the one thing you need to memorize.
直接旋转会变糟——需要记住正确做法。

259
00:52:41,740 --> 00:52:51,210
And let me draw the results. You can also just think of it as redrawing the tree like this. But it's easier from an analysis perspective to think about it as two rotations.
可以看作两次旋转。

260
00:52:51,780 --> 00:53:06,780
Then we can just reduce. As long as we know rotations work, then we know that this thing works. Works meaning it preserves traversal order. And we can maintain all the augmentations. So now if I copy over these labels, the height labels, I have k minus 1. I have for these two guys k minus 1.
旋转有效意味着保持遍历顺序并能维护增广。

261
00:53:09,480 --> 00:53:33,360
And I'm going to do this one. So this is k minus 1. And this is k minus 1. And this is k minus 1. And so this will be k. This will be k. This will be k plus 1. And lo and behold, we have a nice height balance tree in all three cases for this one node. Now this was the lowest node. Once we update this one, it could be that we change the height of the root. Before it was k plus 2.
三种情况都得到高度平衡树。

262
00:53:34,220 --> 00:53:51,350
Now it's k plus 1. Or sometimes we keep it the same, like over in this case. And so now we have to check the parent. Maybe the parent is out of balance. We just keep walking up the node and also maintain all the augmentations as we go. Then we'll keep track of height and subtree size if we want them or any other augmentations.
现在k+1或不变。检查父节点——继续向上走并维护增广。

263
00:53:52,120 --> 00:54:01,840
And after order h operations, we will have restored the height balance property, which means all the way through h equals order log n. And so all of our operations now are magically order log n.
经过O(h)次操作恢复高度平衡——所有操作变为O(log n)。

